{title: The Haven of Rest}
{artist: Henry Gilmour & George Moore}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
My [Eb]soul in sad exile was [Ab]out on life's [Eb]sea, so burdened with sin and dis[Bb]tressed,
till [Eb]I heard a sweet voice saying, "[Ab]Make me your [Eb]choice!" — and I [Ab]entered the [Bb]haven of [Eb]rest.

Chorus
I've [Eb]anchored my soul in the [Ab]haven of [Eb]rest, I'll [Ab]sail the wide [Eb]seas no [Bb]more;
the [Eb]tempest may sweep o'er the [Ab]wild, stormy [Eb]deep — in [Ab]Jesus I'm [Bb]safe ever[Eb]more.
